1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,800
One draws a clue in midair —
the same stroke arrives in a friend's browser.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:06,000
A wrong guess —
and both strokes go coral.

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,800
WRONG · BOTH STROKES GO CORAL

4
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:10,800
The Lens is the referee.

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,800
The right answer lands —
mint, and the word is revealed.

6
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:17,400
The exact path they made
locks into a shared glyph.

7
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,600
No recognition. No redraw.

8
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:25,200
Then they play again — and the painter
picks a new stroke color.

9
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:30,200
WORDLESS was built as a verified loop —

10
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:34,600
prompt, change, simulated Lens Studio Preview,
real browser, test, fix.

11
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:38,200
Hundreds of automated tests
behind one small game.

12
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:41,600
453 AUTOMATED TESTS AT THE PRODUCT FREEZE

13
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:46,200
We measured the relay end to end, rejected
malformed messages without changing the game,

14
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:48,600
and tested the defined round
and recovery transitions.

15
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:50,900
RTT MEDIAN 86 MS · 50/50 PINGS ·
ONE MACHINE, ONE NETWORK (OBSERVED)

16
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:55,000
WORDLESS Relay. Draw in space.
Guess from a browser.

17
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:58,600
Keep the mark you made together.
